23:["$","div",null,{"className":"relative overflow-auto prose-no-margin my-6","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Path"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Requirement"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"content_path"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":["The bulk of the data. On the CAS host, provision ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_bytes"}]," plus headroom. On a worker host, provision ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"twice"}]," the fast tier's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_bytes"}],": the worker creates an executable-variant directory next to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"content_path"}]," that is invisible to the eviction accounting, so that store can reach roughly ",["$","code",null,{"children":"2 × max_bytes"}]," in the worst case."]}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"temp_path"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":["Must be on the ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"same block device"}]," as ",["$","code",null,{"children":"content_path"}],". Otherwise the atomic rename that completes every write degrades to a copy: slower, and it doubles peak space during writes. Everything here is deleted on every startup."]}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["Worker ",["$","code",null,{"children":"work_directory"}]]}],["$","td",null,{"children":["Scratch. Purged at worker startup, which means ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"two workers must never share one."}]," A second worker starting will delete the first worker's in-flight action trees."]}]]}]]}]]}]}]
24:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-50/60 text-foreground dark:bg-amber-500/10","role":"alert","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400","aria-hidden":"true","children":"$1c:props:children:0:props:children"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"Eviction never looks at free space"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Forge evicts on the size it has accounted for, not on the size the\nfilesystem reports, and it evicts only when the store is mutated, never in\nresponse to a failed write. An ",["$","code",null,{"children":"eviction_policy"}]," is optional and its\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_bytes"}]," defaults to zero, which means ",["$","em",null,{"children":"never evict"}],". Leaving it unset on\na ",["$","code",null,{"children":"filesystem"}]," store is the single most common way to fill a disk.\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/runbooks#the-disk-fills-up","children":"Runbooks"}]," has the recovery."]}]]}]]}]
