2e:["$","p",null,{"children":["The path segment after ",["$","code",null,{"children":"scheduler/"}]," is the scheduler's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"name"}]," from the config,\nnot a REAPI instance name. The worker finishes what it has and takes nothing\nnew. What loses work is a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"SIGKILL"}]," (the stop timer firing, or the OOM\nkiller): every in-flight action fails and re-queues, and in this tree a\ndisconnect ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"consumes a retry attempt"}],"; enough of them in a row and the action\nfails outright with a message naming OOM-kill or eviction as the likely cause.\nNote that the admin endpoint is unauthenticated;\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/security-hardening#the-admin-endpoint-has-no-authentication","children":"Security hardening"}],"\nexplains why it must not be routable."]}]
2f:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The CAS"}]," is the safe one. It holds no scheduling state; a restart is a\nwindow of ",["$","code",null,{"children":"UNAVAILABLE"}]," responses and nothing more. Its ",["$","code",null,{"children":"temp_path"}]," is pruned\non the way back up, so a crash mid-write reclaims itself."]}]
